  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466368",
      "title": "Changing the Response Body Type",
      "lectureOrder": 596,
      "videoOrder": 549,
      "sourceHash": "2d24ceca5ae61b300ea272705c2b8f318766486d81ed6acf3c66b7f12dadd517",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 3.797,
          "en": "Instructor: You cannot not only configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.797,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "the observe mode here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.89,
          "en": "you can also configure the response type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.89,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "The default here is JSON, which means the response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 17.46,
          "en": "So the data in the body of your response is JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.46,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "and that tells Angular that it should automatically parse it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 23.31,
          "en": "and convert it to a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.31,
          "end": 26.25,
          "en": "You could, however, also tell Angular, the response type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.25,
          "end": 28.65,
          "en": "will be text, and please keep it as text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.65,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "don't try to convert it to a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 34.8,
          "en": "It could also be a blob if it is a file, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 36.076,
          "en": "The official docs of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.076,
          "end": 38.55,
          "en": "are the place where you can learn all about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 40.86,
          "en": "all available response types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 44.493,
          "en": "So if you use text here and I add a new post here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 47.403,
          "en": "send it first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.75,
          "end": 50.01,
          "en": "Then you still see, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.01,
          "end": 52.47,
          "en": "that I get null here because we had null before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.47,
          "end": 54.91,
          "en": "and even if this is interpreted as a text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.91,
          "end": 56.49,
          "en": "it's still prints null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "However, you can clearly see it is treated as a text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "because it is now wrapped in quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "before it was treated as the null object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "that exists in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 70.11,
          "en": "It becomes even clearer if we try using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.11,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "that here when we get posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "There if I switch the response type to text, we'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "that our application even breaks because it won't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 82.32,
          "en": "if we try to work with a text response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.32,
          "end": 85.05,
          "en": "And I even get an error here because I am using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 87.607,
          "en": "that generic assignment here and I'm saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.607,
          "end": 90.9,
          "en": "\"Hey, the data that is returned here is actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.9,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "of type JavaScript object that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "holds a nested post.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "Well, TypeScript is smart and detects well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "if you tell me that my response data will be of that format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "then it needs to be convertible to a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "If you then also tell me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 108.72,
          "en": "that the response type down there is text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.72,
          "end": 110.43,
          "en": "then you have to be lying somewhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.43,
          "end": 111.96000000000001,
          "en": "because it can't be both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.96000000000001,
          "end": 116.62899999999999,
          "en": "It can't be a string, which is simply not in that format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.62899999999999,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "and such a JavaScript object at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 122.28,
          "en": "So to make this work, we would have to get rid of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.28,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "that generic type assignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 126.72,
          "en": "and now we are allowed to save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.72,
          "end": 129.503,
          "en": "And now of course, you see this breaks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.503,
          "end": 134.31,
          "en": "If I try sending a post and I fetch my post, it breaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.31,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "and I just see these lines because my response here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.407,
          "en": "in the end now treated as a text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.407,
          "end": 146.07,
          "en": "and not as a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.07,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "And actually here it even breaks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 151.02,
          "en": "because the way I try to handle this is not correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.02,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "So I will revert this and I will revert this back to JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "which is the correct data type, which now works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "But it is important to also be aware of this option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "which you can use to tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 166.74,
          "en": "in case you are really getting back some text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.74,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "and you don't want Angular to parse it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "to a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 172.77,
          "en": "Or maybe you are getting back JSON,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 175.32,
          "en": "but you still don't want to let Angular parse it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 177.45,
          "en": "because you wanna parse it on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 180.09,
          "en": "at a later point of time or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 182.76,
          "en": "For this, you can set the response type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "The default is JSON, and most of the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 189,
          "en": "like in probably 99% of all cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "this is the type you wanna keep.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 193.893,
          "en": "So typically you don't need to override that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
